From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 07:13:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: add a bring-up switch to suspend the DCPs
 as for suspend-to-idle

A suspend-to-RAM on the J604 resets the machine about 30 s after the
devices stage resumes (pm_test "devices" with mem; the same stage with
suspend-to-idle survives). One of the suspend-to-RAM-only steps in that
stage is the firmware power-down of the display coprocessors and the
PMP display-sleep arming (iomfb_m4_suspend_firmware()).

Add appledrm.debug_s2r_display_as_idle, default off: when set, a sleep
that powers the SoC down suspends the DCPs as suspend-to-idle does, so
a test can leave that step out. The resume path already handles both.
With the switch off nothing changes.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c | 18 +++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
index 748c0a35d2..f09ff22118 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
@@ -8488,17 +8488,29 @@ bool dcp_s2r_firmware_stopped(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	return READ_ONCE(dcp->s2r_fw_down);
 }
 
+/*
+ * Bring-up: take a sleep that powers the SoC down like suspend-to-idle here:
+ * no firmware power-down of the display coprocessors and no PMP display-sleep
+ * arming. Only for locating a sleep fault; such a sleep cannot complete.
+ * Default off: nothing changes.
+ */
+static bool debug_s2r_display_as_idle;
+module_param(debug_s2r_display_as_idle, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(debug_s2r_display_as_idle,
+		 "Bring-up: suspend the display coprocessors as for suspend-to-idle in a suspend-to-RAM, to locate sleep faults (default: off)");
+
 static int dcp_platform_suspend(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct apple_dcp *dcp = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+	bool fw = pm_suspend_via_firmware() && !READ_ONCE(debug_s2r_display_as_idle);
 
 	/* Its power sequences may crash the DCP and blank the panel. */
 	if (dcp_takeover_was_aborted(dcp))
 		return -EBUSY;
 
-	if (pm_suspend_via_firmware() && dcp_s2r_capable(dcp))
+	if (fw && dcp_s2r_capable(dcp))
 		return dcp_s2r_suspend(dcp);
-	if (pm_suspend_via_firmware() && dcp_s2r_ext_capable(dcp))
+	if (fw && dcp_s2r_ext_capable(dcp))
 		return dcp_s2r_ext_suspend(dcp);
 
 	/*
@@ -8510,7 +8522,7 @@ static int dcp_platform_suspend(struct device *dev)
 	 * down before the freeze (t8132_ext_drm.c). Where that cannot run the
 	 * sleep is refused, as asahi does for G16; suspend-to-idle goes on below.
 	 */
-	if (pm_suspend_via_firmware() && iomfb_is_m4(dcp)) {
+	if (fw && iomfb_is_m4(dcp)) {
 		int ret;
 
 		/* HDMI edges wait for resume, which acts on the level. */
